    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Governance Module Export Issue**: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly from the governance module, but it wasn't being exported. Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` to the finetune/index.js exports.\n\n2. **Toxicity Metric Parameter Issue**: The `toxicityMetric` function was defined to accept `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` was calling it with `(outputs, references)`. This caused references to be incorrectly treated as banned terms, flagging all outputs. Updated the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)` and made it always use the default banned terms, regardless of the second parameter.\n\n3. **Added JSDoc Documentation**: Added proper JSDoc blocks to all public functions in both eval and finetune modules as per code style requirements:\n   - Governance functions: `createGovernanceTemplate`, `validateGovernancePlan`, `calculateReadiness`, `summarizeGovernance`\n   - Eval metrics: `exactMatchMetric`, `toxicityMetric`, `lengthVarianceMetric`\n   - Eval functions: `loadDataset`, `runEvaluations`, `generateReport`, `writeReport`\n\n**Test Results**: All 28 tests passing, including the two that were previously failing:\n- \u2705 src/finetune/governance.test.js - \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"\n- \u2705 src/eval/index.test.js - \"runs default evaluations\"",
